9781	{"artifactId":"LLD-f2f08ccf89f8ab25-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-f2f08ccf89f8ab25-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:controller","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-05T08:01:35.762Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"warn","summary":"review: warn","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"warn","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each of the five decisions of SPEC-1bb064e8e2a1edd1 is designed and built: a fixed per-intent checklist with a threshold, the reviewer probing for itself with insrc analyze, findings identified as does-not-hold or could-not-verify, only does-not-hold blocking, and scope limited to design reviews.","evidence":"Read src/workflow/review/template.ts (two templates, thresholds from settings, isDesignStage limited to design.epic and design.story, the prompt naming insrc_analyze_step), template-review.ts (one session, no extract or per-premise call) and verdict.ts (severityForOutcome returns LOW for anything but does-not-hold).","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"No non-goal is built: a DEF, an ISSUE and a PLAN review is unchanged.","evidence":"git diff from the build's range base 9ce155b to HEAD shows no change to src/workflow/review/extract.ts, probe.ts, verify.ts or resolve.ts. The test 'T12' in src/workflow/review/__tests__/template-review.test.ts pins the sha256 of the extraction prompt for stages define, issue and plan and passes.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"For any stage other than design.epic and design.story, runReview still runs extract, probe and one verify call per premise.","evidence":"src/workflow/review/review.ts: the only new branch is `if (isDesignStage(opts.stage)) return runTemplateReview(artifactMarkdown, opts);` ahead of the unchanged extractClaims, gatherEvidence and verifyClaim loop.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"effectiveReviewVerdict and approveArtifactByJsonPath are unchanged and gate on severity.","evidence":"src/workflow/review/resolve.ts and src/workflow/gates.ts are not in the build's diff. resolve.ts:62 gates on `BLOCKING.has(f.severity)`. The approval tests in src/workflow/review/__tests__/outcome.test.ts (T7) approve a review with only could-not-verify findings and refuse one with a does-not-hold finding.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The reviewer session is a new method beside runEditSession and leaves the one-shot calls and the edit session unchanged.","evidence":"src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts adds runReviewSession, claudeReviewSessionArgs and codexReviewSessionArgs. The test 'one-shot calls and the edit session build the same arguments as before' in src/agent/providers/__tests__/cli-review-session.test.ts records the arguments of complete, completeStructured and runEditSession against a fake binary and they equal the pre-change lists.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Both CLIs run a read-only, tool-using session that returns a schema-checked answer in one run, with the flags the design states.","evidence":"Ran the live test src/agent/providers/__tests__/cli-review-session.live.test.ts with INSRC_LIVE_TESTS=1 on 2026-10-05: both the claude and the codex case passed (read a file, called insrc analyze, no file created, answer matched the schema). The flags in the design equal claudeReviewSessionArgs and codexReviewSessionArgs.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The settings are five designReview.* keys declared in the config catalog and the VS Code manifest and read in template.ts.","evidence":"src/config/config-catalog.ts has 5 designReview entries and vscode-plugin/package.json has 5 insrc.designReview keys (counted with grep). readDesignReviewSettings in template.ts reads them. vscode-plugin/src/config/__tests__/manifest-catalog.test.ts, which requires the manifest to cover the catalog exactly, passes.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The files listed for the controller review surface are the complete set, including every place the phase list is declared.","evidence":"grep for the phase list finds it in src/mcp/server.ts (the phases list and the z.enum), src/mcp/review-step/types.ts and src/mcp/review-step/handler.ts, all listed and all changed; the pinning test src/mcp/__tests__/schema-registry.test.ts was updated. This very review was started through that path: start returned next emit_findings with template design-spec.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.3","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The two listers of findings needing a human behave as the design says: pendingUserFindings leaves out a holds result, and listPendingReviewFindings (the TUI findings view) lists blocking findings only and is unchanged.","evidence":"src/workflow/review/apply.ts filters `f.outcome !== 'holds'` before the fixability filter. src/workflow/review/resolve.ts:47 listPendingReviewFindings filters `f.severity !== 'LOW'` and is called from src/cli/services/workflow.ts:186; resolve.ts is not in the build's diff.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A review record written before this change keeps its counts, verdict, rendering and gate result.","evidence":"verdict.ts returns the three-count shape unless a finding carries an outcome, and report.ts takes the two-list layout only when one does. Test T8 in outcome.test.ts checks counts, verdict, effective verdict, approval and rendering for a record with no outcome fields.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"One deadline covers the whole review: a repeat or a retry gets only the remaining time, a timeout is not retried, and a review past its deadline stamps nothing.","evidence":"template-review.ts computes `limitMs - (nowMs() - startedAt)` before each session and throws before starting one when nothing remains; cli-provider.ts runReviewSession does the same for its one retry and converts the runner's kill into ReviewSessionTimeoutError, which is rethrown, not retried. Covered by T16 in template-review.test.ts and by the deadline tests in cli-review-session.test.ts; 'a failed design review stamps nothing' compares the files byte for byte.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A provider that cannot run a reviewer session fails the review at once with no fallback to the old pipeline.","evidence":"template-review.ts throws 'needs a tool-capable reviewer' when the provider has no runReviewSession function; test T11 asserts the error and that neither complete nor completeStructured was called.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.3","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"When insrc analyze is unavailable inside the session, the review continues and the affected claim is reported as could-not-verify with the reason.","evidence":"Tried: read the prompt in template.ts, which tells the reviewer to continue with file reads and search and to say what was missing. Nothing in code enforces this and no test runs a session with the insrc server absent, so the behaviour rests on the reviewer model following the instruction. Missing: a live run with the insrc MCP server unregistered or the daemon stopped.","action":"Either accept this as prompt-level behaviour, or add a live test that runs a reviewer session without the insrc server.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every acceptance criterion ac1 to ac5 maps to at least one test, and every test the design names exists and passes.","evidence":"The mapping lists T1 to T18 with none unmapped. The test files outcome.test.ts, template.test.ts, template-review.test.ts, cli-review-session.test.ts and review-step-findings.test.ts carry them by number. Suites run on 2026-10-05: workflow 1414, MCP 286, CLI 167, agent 82 with no failures; the gated live test T14 was run separately and passed for both CLIs.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":14,"unverified":1},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-05T08:01:35.762Z","model":"client"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
